WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.453
The first change is small but essential:

2
00:00:02.453 --> 00:00:06.021
a patch owner column in the
configuration database export,

3
00:00:06.021 --> 00:00:10.900
right beside the configuration owner, with
the onboarding wave after the region.

4
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.175
The guide had named that field, but
the sample export never carried it.

5
00:00:15.175 --> 00:00:20.191
Look at the server on Amazon's cloud:
Ansible configures it and patches it,

6
00:00:20.191 --> 00:00:24.538
but it still goes to Arc, for
inventory, assessment and Defender.

7
00:00:24.538 --> 00:00:26.563
Its patch owner tag says Ansible,

8
00:00:26.563 --> 00:00:29.863
so Update Manager assesses
it and schedules nothing.

9
00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:35.400
And because this is a GCC estate, the
sample now uses commercial regions.
